      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "The statement $\\sim(p \\leftrightarrow \\sim q)$ is equivalent to:",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "$p \\leftrightarrow q$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "$p \\leftrightarrow \\sim q$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "$\\sim p \\leftrightarrow q$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "$\\sim p \\leftrightarrow \\sim q$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "$p \\leftrightarrow \\sim q$ is true if $p$ and $\\sim q$ have same truth values (i.e., opposite truth values of $p$ and $q$).\nThus, $\\sim(p \\leftrightarrow \\sim q)$ is true when $p$ and $q$ have the same truth values.\nThis is the definition of $p \\leftrightarrow q$."
    },
    {
      "ref": "MATH-MRE-002",
      "subtopic": "tautology-fallacy",
      "type": "single_correct",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "expected_time_sec": 80,
      "source_type": "pyq",
      "exam": "jee_main",
      "year": 2022,
      "shift": "25 Jul 2022, Shift 1",
      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "The statement $(\\sim p \\wedge q) \\implies (p \\vee \\sim q)$ is equivalent to:",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "$p \\vee \\sim q$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "$\\sim p \\vee q$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "$p \\wedge \\sim q$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "$\\sim p \\wedge q$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Using $A \\implies B \\equiv \\sim A \\vee B$:\n$\\sim (\\sim p \\wedge q) \\vee (p \\vee \\sim q) \\equiv (p \\vee \\sim q) \\vee (p \\vee \\sim q) \\equiv p \\vee \\sim q$."
    }
  ]
